NNAAMMEE
       lvremove - remove a logical volume

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       llvvrreemmoovvee [-A|--autobackup y|n] [-d|--debug] [-f|--force] [-h|-?|--help]
       [-t|--test] [-v|--verbose] LogicalVolumePath [LogicalVolumePath...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       llvvrreemmoovvee removes one or more logical volumes.  Confirmation will be re‐
       quested before deactivating any active logical volume prior to removal.
       Logical  volumes  cannot  be deactivated or removed while they are open
       (e.g. if they contain a mounted filesystem).  Removing an origin  logi‐
       cal volume will also remove all dependent snapshots.

       If  the  logical volume is clustered then it must be deactivated on all
       nodes in the cluster before it can be removed. A single  lvchange  com‐
       mand issued from one node can do this.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       See llvvmm(8) for common options.

       _-_f_, _-_-_f_o_r_c_e
              Remove active logical volumes without confirmation.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       Remove  the  active  logical  volume lvol1 in volume group vg00 without
       asking for confirmation:

            llvvrreemmoovvee ‐‐ff vvgg0000//llvvooll11

       Remove all logical volumes in volume group vg00:

            llvvrreemmoovvee vvgg0000

